\section{Related Work}
\label{sec:related}

\subsection{Mixture-of-Experts (MoE)}
MoE models activate a subset of parameters per input, reducing
compute while scaling capacity \cite{jacobs1991,shazeer2017,fedus2022}.
Recent work includes Mixtral \cite{jiang2024}, DeepSeek-MoE
\cite{dai2024}, and Switch Transformer \cite{fedus2022}.
\textbf{Key limitation:} experts are fixed at initialization.

\subsection{Continual Learning}
Addresses catastrophic forgetting through regularization
(EWC \cite{kirkpatrick2017}), parameter isolation
(PackNet \cite{mallya2018}), or replay \cite{lopezpaz2017}.
\textbf{Key limitation:} reduces forgetting but cannot prove
zero.

\subsection{Neural Architecture Search (NAS)}
Automates architecture design \cite{zoph2017,elsken2019}.
Dynamic variants include Net2Net \cite{chen2016} and DEN
\cite{yoon2018}. \textbf{Key limitation:} growth triggered by
loss, not by knowledge saturation.

\subsection{Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)}
Augments LLMs with external retrieval \cite{lewis2020,guu2020,borgeaud2022}.
\textbf{Key limitation:} does not modify model weights.

\subsection{Biology-Inspired Neural Networks}
NEAT \cite{stanley2002}, CPPN \cite{stanley2007}, NCA
\cite{mordvintsev2020}. \textbf{Key limitation:} not applied
to billion-parameter language models.

