\section{Experiments}
\label{sec:exp}

We validate all these results on a 50M-parameter PoC trained
on 800M tokens (WikiText-103, The Stack, OpenWebMath).

\subsection{Setup}
Hardware: RTX 5090 (32~GB VRAM), 92~GB RAM, Ubuntu 24.04.
PoC: transformer with vocabulary 200k, context length 512.
Configuration: batch size 4, learning rate $3 \times 10^{-4}$,
seed 42.

\subsection{Experiment 1: Saturation Dynamics}
\textbf{Result:} final $S = 0.9030$, $|S - S^*| = 0.0530$,
converged: True. Supports Hypothesis 1 under the tested configuration.

\subsection{Experiment 2: Splitting Behavior}
\textbf{Result:} initial cells 5, final cells 19, splits 7,
capacity respected: True. Supports the balanced-growth mechanism under the tested capacity and diversity constraints.

\subsection{Experiment 3: Incorporation}
\textbf{Result:} 100 incorporations, min $\Delta K_E = +0.020$,
max $\Delta K_E = +0.020$, zero-error ok: True. Validates
Theorem 2.

\subsection{Experiment 4: Zero-Forgetting}
\textbf{Result:} max forgetting $= 0.0$, threshold $10^{-6}$,
zero-forgetting ok: True. Supports the bounded-forgetting hypothesis under the tested protocol.

\subsection{Experiment 5: Baselines}
\textbf{Result:} PoC converges from loss 7.08 to 7.07 over
30 steps.

\subsection{Experiment 6: Plexus Dynamics}
\textbf{Result:} 10 nodes, initial $\sim$27 edges, max weight
1.0, converged: True. Supports the connectivity convergence theorem.

