\subsection{What Would Falsify the Approach?}

Any of the following:
\begin{itemize}
    \item A run where $S > 0.9$ for 100 steps without a split.
    \item An incorporation with $\Delta K < -10^{-5}$.
    \item A task with $F_j > 10^{-6}$.
    \item Cell count exceeding $C$ by any margin.
    \item Plexus weights diverging under stated assumptions.
\end{itemize}

None observed in the PoC.

\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:concl}

We presented Berna R5, an architecture for language models
that grow, correct locally, and bound forgetting under the tested protocol. Grounded in
two theorems with complete proofs, two design invariants, and two empirical hypotheses, validated on a
50M-parameter PoC across six experiments.

Core ideas: knowledge as a 6D knowledge state space; cells that are born,
split, die; a 100-chromosome DNA Kernel; a plexus of dynamic
edges; a federation with SQL lineage; and a Fail-Closed Integrity Invariant.

All code, proofs, and configurations are released at
\url{https://github.com/Berna-Labs/berna-r5-poc}.

\section{Limitations}
\label{sec:limits}

We document limitations explicitly.

\textbf{Theoretical.} Hypothesis 1 uses a simplified
Lagrangian; rigorous treatment requires KKT analysis.
Hypothesis 1 part (ii) assumes split decreases loss.
Theorem 1 (balanced growth) has a benefit function that is
qualitative. Theorem 2 (plexus connectivity) has a scale-free
property that is empirical.

\textbf{Empirical.} All experiments at 50M. Behavior at 1.5B
untested. Baselines on real benchmarks not run. Other domains
(medical, legal, multilingual) untested.

\textbf{Design.} 100 chromosomes justified information-theoretically
but not optimized. 6 dimensions is a modeling decision.
Constants chosen heuristically.

\textbf{Deployment.} Multi-node federation untested. Hardware
compatibility beyond RTX 5090 untested.

\textbf{What this paper does NOT claim.} SOTA on any benchmark.
Superiority over GPT-4-class models. Scalability beyond 1.5B.
Optimality of any design choice. Completeness of any proof
(assumptions are explicit).

\textbf{What this paper DOES claim.} A novel architecture
combining dynamic knowledge cells, plexus connectivity,
federation, transactional incorporation, protected retention,
and growth control. Two mathematical results with explicit
assumptions and proofs, two design invariants enforced by
system design, and two empirical hypotheses evaluated on a
small-scale PoC. Six reproducible experiments on one GPU.
Bounded forgetting was observed under the tested continual-
learning protocol. Open-source, hardware-adaptive.
Falsifiability: any result can be refuted by a single
counterexample or a failed replication.

